(text "Reference designator -> part value\n(switches, J1/J2 and the unnumbered regulator are left out, as on the original)\n\nC9, C10  ->  33uF\nC1, C2, C5 THRU C7, C11 THRU C22  ->  0.1uF\nR2, R6, R7, R10, R11, R13 THRU R15, R60  ->  1K\nR1  ->  270K\nCR1  ->  1N914\nU17, U20, U23  ->  74123\nR3 THRU R5, R8, R9, R12  ->  47K\nC3, C8  ->  0.001uF\nC4  ->  0.01uF\nU18, U19, U22  ->  74107\nU9  ->  74LS30\nU10  ->  7404\nU11  ->  74LS10\nU12  ->  7410\nU13, U16  ->  7402\nU14, U25  ->  7400\nU8, U15  ->  74LS04\nU15.5  ->  7427\nU21  ->  7430\nU24  ->  8T97\nU1, U3, U4, U6, U7  ->  7405\nU2  ->  DATA HEADER SOCKET\nU5  ->  8212\nR16 THRU R59  ->  220\nLA0 THRU LA15, LD0 THRU LD7, LHT1, LIE1, LO0 THRU LO7, LRN1, LS0 THRU LS7, LWT1  ->  LED'S" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 855 30 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ce5c4b78-9dba-52d2-aa87-14555ca72192"))
(text "Transcribed from the 600 dpi scan of IMSAI drawing \"IMSAI 8080 SYSTEM CPA REV. 4\" ((c) 1977 IMSAI Mfg. Corp.).\nRevisions on the drawing: 0 original 12/75, 1 ECN76-0051 & ECO77-0039 (11/76, 4/77), 2 ECO77-0098 (8/77).\nThe blocks follow the original sheet: control on the left, gating and address lamps in the middle,\ncable socket and lamps on the right, regulator along the bottom. Wires are net labels, not traced.\n~{X} means X is active low.\n\nScan ambiguities and how they were resolved:\n1. U13 pin 12 and U15.5 (7427) pin 2 form a net without a driver on the drawing. The wire crosses the\n   U14 pin 8 -> U15 pin 5 wire without a junction dot. Connected to U14 pin 8 (EXAM_ACTIVE = examine\n   sequence running) because the examine logic only works that way. INFERRED, not visible on the scan.\n2. U22 pin 6 (RUN flip-flop Q-bar) is drawn continuously connected to the T5 line (R60 pull-up, bus pin 20,\n   J/K and clear inputs). Parastream describes T5 as a plain tie-high line. As drawn, T5 is high while\n   stopped and low while running (the RUN lamp LRN hangs on it). Note: T5 loads U22 with ~17 TTL inputs.\n3. The DO5 input of the stop logic (U11 pin 9) is marked \"37\" on the scan; pin 37 is A10, DO5 is pin 39.\n4. U25 pin 5 is connected to ~{SOUT} (U15 pin 2), following the ~{SOUT} label on that wire.\n5. Lamp \"LHT\" on the drawing is called \"LHD\" in the parts list.\n6. U15.5 is the reference used on the original (7427 added by an engineering change).\n7. U27 (7805), J2 (wire flags A/B) and #FLG are not numbered on the original. The lamps LIE, LHT, LWT\n   and LRN are named LIE1, LHT1, LWT1 and LRN1 because KiCad references need a number.\n8. Parts shown with 74LS symbols carry the original type as value (7400, 7402, 7404, 7405, 7410, 7427,\n   7430, 74107, 74123). 8T97 uses the pin-compatible 74LS367 symbol; its pin 15 is not shown on the drawing.\n9. Unused gate inputs are left open as on the original.\n\nIEEE-696 notes (parastream): cut bus pin 20 (T5 / UNPROT) and pin 53 (~{SSW_DSB}) on IEEE-696 systems;\nthe CP-A expects ~{POC} (pin 99) during ~{PRESET} (pin 75)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 855 560 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left top)) (uuid "abf19d00-1476-5fc1-8a5a-ab95bac57448"))
